NAME
     unshare - run a program in new namespaces

SYNOPSIS
     unshare [-u] [-p] [-m] [-U] [-n] [-f] [COMMAND [ARG...]]

DESCRIPTION
     unshare runs COMMAND (a shell by default) with namespaces of its
     own, so that what it does to the hostname, to process numbers, to
     mounts, to user ids or to the network is its own business and not
     the machine's.

OPTIONS
     -u, --uts     a hostname of its own
     -p, --pid     process numbers of its own; wants -f
     -m, --mount   a mount table of its own
     -U, --user    user ids of its own, and it starts as root in them
     -n, --net     a network of its own: interfaces, routes, sockets
     -f, --fork    fork before running, which a new pid namespace needs

EXAMPLES
     unshare -u sh -c 'hostname other; hostname'
     unshare -pf /bin/ps

SEE ALSO
     nsenter(1), vmm(1), /proc/PID/ns
